## 12. SYSTEM REVISION HISTORY AND DEVELOPMENT LOG

### July 2, 2026 - Session 1 Briefing
- Primary Objective: Consolidate Phase 1, fix Canonical Signature compile bug, address Hyper-V blank screen, establish automated development checkpoint ruleset.
- Changes Made:
  - .github/workflows/build-kernel.yml: Refactored into dependent multi-job workflow compile_kernel then publish_release. Extended execution limits to 360 minutes. Integrated libdw-dev rsync kmod dependencies. Added storage cleaning step to prevent disk exhaustion.
  - scripts/auto-build.sh: Full automation using gh CLI API. Dynamic workspace path detection eliminating case sensitivity collisions.
  - rootfs/usr/bin/xeno-start-hyprland: VM detection script with automatic software rendering environment variable export.
  - rootfs/etc/systemd/system/xeno-session.service: Reconfigured to execute through xeno-start-hyprland wrapper.
  - iso/build/boot/grub/grub.cfg: Added hostname=xeno-os parameter to prevent Casper resetting hostname to ubuntu.
  - rootfs packages: Added tmux, alsa-utils, micro, fzf.
- Compilation Outcome: Workflow compiled, packages generated without warnings, ISO packaged as xeno_os-alpha-v_02.0.iso.
- Tested In: Microsoft Hyper-V Gen 2 UEFI and VirtualBox VMSVGA plus 3D.
- Diagnostic Findings: VM boots into live compositor on TTY1 without blank screen. Hostname correctly registers as xeno-os. Hyper-V core communication modules load natively.
- Next Steps: Awaiting user verification and direct instruction to initiate Phase 2.

### July 6, 2026 - Session 2 Briefing
- Primary Objective: Decouple design language from hardcoded values so the user defines all colors, typography, and spacing themselves rather than the AI presupposing them.
- Changes Made:
  - .cursorrules Section 1: Added Rule 7 forbidding inline/invented design values; AI must import from the central theme module or ask.
  - .cursorrules Section 3: Added desktop/theme.py and desktop/shell/theme.ts to the project layout as the single source of truth.
  - .cursorrules Section 5, Guardrail A: Added theme import as a mandatory step in the panel import order.
  - .cursorrules Section 5, Guardrail B: Added theme import to the Astal v2 enforced snippet.
  - .cursorrules Section 5, Guardrail C: Generalized the VM-rendering rule to reference a theme opacity token instead of a literal rgba value.
  - .cursorrules Section 6: Replaced the fixed color/typography/spacing values with an empty token schema (all `None`/`undefined`) in `theme.py` and `theme.ts`, to be filled in by the user; updated the PySide6 stylesheet template to reference `theme.*` dynamically.
  - .cursorrules Section 7: Rewrote base_panel.py to import `theme` instead of defining local XENO_* constants.
  - .cursorrules Section 8: Reordered inventory so the theme files are built and filled in before base_panel.py.
- Compilation Outcome: Not applicable — documentation/rules change only, no code executed or built this session.
- Tested In: Not applicable.
- Diagnostic Findings: Not applicable.
- Next Steps: User defines actual values in desktop/theme.py and desktop/shell/theme.ts before any panel or shell code is generated against them.